&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;**If you’re interested in joining the Druva family in a future Sales Development Representative role in Santa Clara, CA, please join our talent community. Submit your resume below, and a recruiter will review and reach out when we have an opportunity arise that matches your skillset &amp;amp; interests. This post is not in reference to a currently open position, but rather in anticipation of future business need.**&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva, the autonomous data security company, puts data security on autopilot with a 100% SaaS, fully managed platform to secure and recover data from all threats. The Druva Data Security Cloud ensures the availability, confidentiality, and fidelity of data - providing customers with autonomous protection, rapid incident response, and guaranteed data recovery. The company is trusted by its more than 6,000 customers, including 65 of the Fortune 500, to defend business data in today’s ever-connected world. Amidst a rapidly evolving security landscape, Druva offers a $10 million Data Resiliency Guarantee ensuring customer data is protected and secured against every cyber threat. Visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;druva.com&lt;/a&gt; and follow us on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;What we would be looking for in the future when a Sales Development Representative &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;position opens up:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role &amp;amp; The Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to be an influential member of a high performing sales team at a fast-growing SaaS company. As an SDR you’ll work closely with our sales and marketing teams to drive new business by evangelizing Druva’s technology to prospective customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Customer Marketing and Sales teams to drive attendance to customer events and webinars&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Following up on customer alerts, leads and requests with the goal of identifying upsell/x-sell opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Processing customer leads/contacts through Outreach sequences (cold-calling to new customer contacts/leads is required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule customer meetings and product demos for Account Executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with marketing, sales, and business development on email messaging and talk tracks for specific use-cases, events and webinars&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as liaison between Customer Marketing and owners of customer accounts, while acting as a dynamic feedback loop&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage inbound leads process to maximize conversion and pipeline development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand Druva’s offerings and competitive positioning to effectively communicate and apply them to a prospects needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to apply a hunter mind-set to work strategically with AEs on campaigns to promote x-sell/upsell opportunities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurately enter, update, and maintain daily activity and prospect information in SFDC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve and exceed monthly quotas and objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of prior SDR experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience/awareness/knowledge of technology solutions, cloud and Saas preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with tools such as SFDC, CL, Salesloft, Linkedin, Zoom, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CRM fluency - ability to create reports is a plus!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to articulate technical capabilities in terms of business value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong desire to learn a comprehensive software sales process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applies strategic thinking to uncover additional stakeholders and prospects within existing customer accounts to support account growth and retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sense of urgency and motivation to meet and exceed aggressive goal&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to make cold calls and initiate conversations with install base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication and presentation skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A plus if you are hard working, competitive, professional and comfortable taking direction and feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This post is not in reference to a currently open position.&lt;/strong&gt; However, if this position were to open, it would align with the compensation information below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The pay range for this position is expected to be between $88,000 and $117,333/year; however, base pay offered may vary depending on multiple individualized, non-discriminatory factors, including market location, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package for this position may also include other incentive compensation opportunities in the form of discretionary annual bonus or commissions, and equity. Additionally, full-time employees are eligible to participate in our comprehensive benefits program, including health and wellness benefits, 401(k) retirement plan, life and disability insurance coverages, and other benefits the Company may offer from time to time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;br&gt;Visit druva.com and follow us on LinkedIn, X and Facebook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Druva is seeking to hire a Sales Engineer with a focus on Data Protection with AI &amp;amp;amp;Data Security. As a Sales Engineer, you will provide technical direction and business guidance to the regional sales teams. We are looking for a motivated and proactive&lt;br&gt;individual to help exceed sales targets by driving innovative technical programs, conducting customer demonstrations, POCs, and overseeing daily technical solutioning activities. You will be responsible for evangelizing, positioning, and&lt;br&gt;architecting Druva’s Data Protection, AI &amp;amp;amp; Data Security Solutions to a mix of new &amp;amp;amp; existing customer accounts in the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrates technical leadership and subject matter expertise on fully managed cloud-native SaaS, Endpoint &amp;amp;amp; Server Data Protection, AI &amp;amp;amp; Data Security, and Cyber Resiliency&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Provides technical leadership and direction to customers and internal staff in the development of Druva solutions, supporting pre-sales activities within the assigned region&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Leverage technical discovery and qualification fundamentals to establish rapport as a trusted advisor to develop and propose solutions that meet the technology and business requirements of prospective &amp;amp;amp; existing customer accounts in the region&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Meet business objectives by collaborating with Sales Executives in the region&lt;br&gt;• Assist in delivering technical enablement to the Druva Channel Partner ecosystem&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp;5 &amp;nbsp;to 8 years in technical customer-facing roles with at least 2+ years as a sales engineer working with enterprise software solutions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Intermediate-level knowledge of enterprise server backup technologies&lt;br&gt;• Intermediate-level knowledge of Virtualization Platforms VMWare, HyperV, Nutanix &amp;amp;amp; ProxMox.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Intermediate-level knowledge of Databases such as MS-SQL, Oracle, Azure SQL.&lt;br&gt;• Working knowledge &amp;amp;amp; understanding of AI concepts and tools. Hands on knowledge of Claude, Copilot would be added advantage.&lt;br&gt;• Intermediate level knowledge of operating systems, including MS Windows, Linux,&amp;amp; amp; macOS.&lt;br&gt;• Experience with Active Directory, Entra ID, SSO, MFA, SCCM, and automated deployment tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Intermediate level of knowledge of industry AI.&lt;br&gt;• Basic understanding of network technologies and protocols – TCP/IP, VLAN, DNS, switches, firewalls, routers, and proxies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Entrepreneurial - willing to go the extra mile, strong work ethic, resourceful, “get it&lt;br&gt;done” attitude&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• A highly energetic drive to meet goals with a strong hands-on, “can-do” approach&lt;br&gt;• Strives in moving in a fast-paced environment, including handling multiple calls/demos per day with immediate follow-up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Intermediate-level knowledge of Cloud platforms like Azure &amp;amp;amp; AWS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shift Timing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The role requires working in the US time zone, with shift timings from 6:00 PM to 3:00 AM IST.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Skills And Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Experience with a SaaS company or demonstrable knowledge of SaaS practices&lt;br&gt;• Intermediate level of knowledge of cloud-native IaaS &amp;amp;amp; PaaS services.&lt;br&gt;• A high level of business acumen and experience working with various cross-&lt;br&gt;functional stakeholders to foster collaboration in solving business challenges&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Fundamental knowledge of the NIST Cybersecurity 2.0 framework&lt;br&gt;Basic knowledge of cybersecurity solutions in the areas of EDR, XDR, MDR, etc.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits on a highly collaborative, performance-driven Commercial sales team focused on helping customers modernize data protection and cyber resilience with Druva’s 100% SaaS platform. The Account Executive owns the territory end-to-end, maintaining and expanding existing customer relationships while actively hunting and closing net-new logos.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work in a true two-in-a-box model with a dedicated local Systems Engineer to drive deep discovery, strong customer engagement, and a consultative sales motion across the full lifecycle, from prospecting through expansion. This is a high-impact role for someone who thrives on territory ownership, values teamwork, and enjoys building durable customer relationships while driving new growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose &amp;amp; Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own and execute the go-to-market strategy for the assigned Commercial territory, managing a defined book of business while identifying, prospecting, and closing new customer opportunities across organizations with 251–2,999 employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build trusted relationships with IT and security leaders by understanding their business challenges and aligning them to Druva’s cloud-native data protection and cyber resilience platform. Partnering closely with a dedicated local Systems Engineer, you will lead discovery, technical validation, and solution design to clearly articulate the value of a SaaS-based approach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate cross-functionally with Customer Success, Channel Partners, and internal teams to support onboarding, adoption, renewals, and expansion, while building pipeline, forecasting accurately, and consistently delivering against revenue targets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect and close new sales opportunities in a defined territory and a defined set of target accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate results; consistent, reliable performance with 100% minimum attainment expected&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the local, regional and national channel&amp;nbsp;partners to drive awareness and &quot;buzz&quot; in your territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arrange and&amp;nbsp;help conduct&amp;nbsp;initial product demonstrations and presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage sales process and opportunity closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing account management to ensure customer satisfaction and to drive&amp;nbsp;additional cross-sell/up-sell opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of Field Account Executive experience with documented quota attainment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales experience in the IT or technology industry preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build executive-level relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous learner&amp;nbsp;and student of the game - you want to constantly get better&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand the &quot;bigger picture&quot; and the business drivers around IT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You strive for greatness and push yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to professionalism, integrity, and positive team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree or equivalent&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like in this Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success means consistently owning and growing the assigned Commercial territory through predictable, high-quality execution. You effectively balance expanding existing accounts with adding new logos, building trusted relationships with IT and security leaders and positioning Druva as a strategic partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You operate as a strong partner to your dedicated Systems Engineer, lead disciplined discovery, guide customers through value-based buying decisions, and maintain a healthy, well-managed pipeline with accurate forecasts. You collaborate closely with Customer Success and channel partners to drive renewals, expansions, and long-term retention.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are also a dependable, high-integrity team member who shows up prepared, contributes to a strong team culture, and helps elevate the overall performance of the Commercial Central Team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Innovation is how we operate, not a side project. You’ll work in a culture that values bold thinking and continuous improvement, where global teams experiment, iterate, and turn new ideas into products customers can rely on.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for high-ownership work, visible impact, and a culture that values innovation, collaboration, accountability, and growth—where you’ll be trusted to lead and empowered to build—you’ll thrive at Druva.&lt;/p&gt;
