&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position is on a hybrid schedule, minimum Tues./Wed./Thurs. at Druva&#39;s Santa Clara HQ office.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose &amp;amp; Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Manager, Corporate FP&amp;amp;A owns Druva&#39;s consolidated financial picture: the total company P&amp;amp;L, cash flow, balance sheet forecast and long-range plan. You&#39;ll report to the VP of Finance and lead a small, high-impact team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on leadership role at the center of the finance organization. You&#39;ll pull inputs from GTM, R&amp;amp;D, G&amp;amp;A and cost of revenue planning into one integrated view of the business. You&#39;ll own the company-level forecast and the Annual Operating Plan (AOP) consolidation, and build the financial narrative for the CFO, the executive team and the board.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be joining at a moment of real opportunity: we&#39;re refreshing our planning processes, raising the bar on forecast accuracy, and using AI to make FP&amp;amp;A faster and more insightful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Corporate FP&amp;amp;A team at Druva serves as the strategic engine for the company&#39;s financial growth. The team is highly visible and deeply collaborative, partnering directly with executive leadership, the board, and global business units to translate complex data into actionable strategies. Driven by a low-ego, high-ownership mindset, the team&#39;s culture balances rigorous, data-backed financial discipline with rapid execution to support Druva&#39;s scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Total company P&amp;amp;L and forecast&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the consolidated company forecast, from revenue through operating income, on a monthly and quarterly cadence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consolidate inputs from GTM, R&amp;amp;D, G&amp;amp;A and cost of revenue planning into one integrated, tied-out view&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead forecast and actuals reviews with the VP Finance and CFO, focused on drivers, risks and opportunities rather than just the numbers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Controller&#39;s team on close timing, actuals and reconciliation to forecast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cash and balance sheet&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the cash flow forecast, including collections, payables, bonus payouts and other timing items&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecast key balance sheet items such as deferred revenue, receivables and working capital&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support capital allocation decisions with clear scenario analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Long-range plan and AOP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the multi-year long-range plan (LRP) and its link to the company&#39;s growth, margin and cash targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead AOP consolidation: the framework, calendar, top-down targets and the integrated three-statement plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scenario and sensitivity models for strategic decisions and board discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Board and executive reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the financial sections of quarterly board decks and memos: results, rest-of-year outlook, and plan framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure every number ties out and the story is clear, credible and decision-oriented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond quickly and accurately to ad hoc requests from the VP Finance, CFO, CEO and board members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team and systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach and develop a high-impact team, setting a high bar for accuracy, timeliness and business insight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the integrated three-statement model and the planning architecture behind it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI and automation to cut manual work, shorten the forecast cycle and support a faster close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of progressive FP&amp;amp;A experience, including at least 3 years leading FP&amp;amp;A teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a B2B SaaS or subscription software company, with a strong command of SaaS metrics, deferred revenue, and how bookings flow through to revenue and cash&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ownership of the consolidated company forecast and AOP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and maintaining a long-range plan used by the VP Finance, CFO and board&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep three-statement modeling skills across an integrated P&amp;amp;L, balance sheet and cash flow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing board-level materials and presenting directly to a CFO and executive team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of improving forecast accuracy and planning efficiency through better models, systems or automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical use of AI tools in FP&amp;amp;A workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise communication, with the judgment to push back on assumptions and stand behind a number&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with a planning platform such as Adaptive, Anaplan or Pigment, and with BI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a late-stage private or public company, including investor or lender reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to treasury, cash management or debt financing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or CPA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like in the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;First 90 days&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the monthly company forecast and cash forecast end to end, with no gaps in delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted working relationships with the VP Finance, CFO, Controller and FP&amp;amp;A leads across GTM and corporate functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver the financial sections of the next quarterly board package on time and fully tied out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;First 6–12 months&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead AOP consolidation to an on-time, board-approved plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Refresh the long-range plan and align it with the AOP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measurably improve forecast accuracy for operating income and cash&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the integrated three-statement model with documented processes and backup coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Innovation is how we operate, not a side project. You’ll work in a culture that values bold thinking and continuous improvement, where global teams experiment, iterate, and turn new ideas into products customers can rely on.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for high-ownership work, visible impact, and a culture that values innovation, collaboration, accountability, and growth—where you’ll be trusted to lead and empowered to build—you’ll thrive at Druva.&lt;/p&gt;
